Hold the account's keys to Vim's in inlyne's own tests

The keys the settings bind were checked only by how the keys page drew
them, so a binding inlyne read otherwise, or q closing it again, passed.
The build now names the settings' keys, and a test presses Vim's keys
through them: q and Escape alone do nothing, and :q and Return, ZZ and
Space w close it.

